WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:05.590
In Paris, your React app renders English
for a browser that asks for French.

2
00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:09.770
Its only text is English, and
the app loads no other language.

3
00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:15.700
General Translation lets you initialize
gt-react before the app renders and wrap

4
00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:17.190
its text in T.

5
00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:23.070
List your languages in gt.config.json,
and add a loadTranslations file.

6
00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:29.510
An entry file calls initializeGTSPA
first, then loads the rest of the app.

7
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.650
Wrap the page's text in
T, so the CLI finds it.

8
00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:38.710
Sign in, set your project ID,
and run npx gt translate.

9
00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:42.570
Spanish, Japanese or French
loads before the app renders,

10
00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:45.030
and in Paris it opens in French.
